v0.20.0 (2026-09-14)

Deathmatch is the last major feature before v1.0, 
so until then, only polish and fixes.

And yes: Replays broke again. BUT you can now record hours of gameplay in
slaughter-maps without fear that the replay become too big in memory :)

Features and improvements
  - multiplayer: 
    - deathmatch! the classic altdeath rules: no monsters, all
      keys, weapons taken, items back after 30 s, random deathmatch starts,
      no fog of war, kills on the scoreboard, kill and time limits
    - friendly fire as a host option for coop
    - a player teleporting onto another player telefrags them
    - Boom's not-in-coop / not-in-deathmatch thing flags are honoured
    - the host needs a second player to start
    - leaving a game, or the host closing the room, ends it and returns
      to the menu
    - your colour can be changed in the lobby
  - menu: 
    - reworked status messages
    - select arrows and number steppers in the menu's own colours
    - F5 with the menu open reloads without asking
  - HUD messages over the status bar; a repeated line counts up (x2); 
    Settings > Visuals > Messages picks all / MP only / off
  - the pickup puff is drawn in the item fog's own art (IFOG), shrinking around
    where the item stood, and for every player's pickups in a network game
    - the item fog and the pickup puff cast a blue light
      (TopDOOM's own GLDEFS addition)
  - players gib when a hit leaves them below -100 health
  - DEHACKED: 
    - Frame records retime or redraw the teleport and item fogs, and the
      pickup puff with the item fog
    - GOT* pickup strings apply

Fixed bugs
  - the teleport fog plays vanilla's full chain: the opening A,B,A,B flicker
    was missing, so it ran 60 tics instead of 72
  - a respawning ceiling-hung item's fog sits on the floor, as in vanilla
  - the high death cry (pdiehi) plays in DOOM2 only
  - health and armor no longer carry fractions
  - R after a death no longer reloads a level-entry another tab wrote
  - R after taking over a replay that jumped to another level reloads the 
    right level
  - fixed bugs regarding tracers and projectiles 
    (I thought we fiexd long ago -.-)
  - a lift no longer carries a monster into the ceiling when the monster's
    box reaches onto it across a narrow strip
  - a monster perched on a ledge corner above the floor under it, no longer
    freezes there


