v0.19.1 (2026-09-12)

Replays break, but I am quiet confident everything is in it's right place now.
Next: Deathmatch

Features and improvements
  - multiplayer: hold TAB for the scoreboard, which lists every player's
    kills and ping. Intermission also shows it above the level's stats.
  - replay: switch between players

Fixed bugs
  - multiplayer: players in parts of a map joined only by teleporters no longer
    desync over what auto-aim may lock onto
  - bars on a rising lift no longer vanish when the player stands behind them
  - a faded grate or fence now dithers instead of vanishing


===============================================================================

v0.19.0 (2026-09-11)

This was supposed to become v0.18.2, but a lot more changes came together 
plus a replay format break.
Then I checked what would be required for multiplayer... which would have lead 
to more replay/save breaks, so... I followed through with it!

Features and improvements
  - initial MULTIPLAYER: Co-op only, so far!
  - replays
    - replay files are about a quarter smaller: the camera and aim columns are
      stored against a linear prediction, the desync samples as rounded columns
    - replays now store an additional keyframe after level change
    - the replay track's hover label names the level a jump would land in,
      when the recording spans more than one
    - "Play" on a replay is hold-to-confirm while a game is running; over a
      playing replay, Play, Load and Start new game are plain clicks again
  - reworked tops on crates and pillars
    - the level's own wall masses only get one where they end at a single
      height all round
    - can be switched off under Settings -> Visuals -> Top-down extras
      (requires level reload)
  - menues & WAD Library
    - "Start new game" only shows on the New Game tab, which is now accented
    - status messages now read amber, errors still red
    - hiding thin ceiling steps can now be switched off under
      Settings -> Visuals -> Top-down extras (also requires level reload)
    - the WAD Library no longer prints "game WAD" against every row of the
      Game WADs folder
    - a WAD row with no refusal to show no longer reserves the badge column's
      width, in the WAD Library and the add-on list alike
    - a first start now opens on a preselected WAD set,
      configurable in constants.ts
  - F5 does not immediately reload the app during gameplay
  - a collected item now leaves a small translucent puff where it stood,
    switchable under Settings -> Visuals -> Top-down extras
  - added IDCLEV cheat to warp to any map of the loaded set 
    (replaces the dev-mode's N/P map jump)
  - the status text's debug lines are now a setting of their own
  - sleeping monsters idle on the spot as in vanilla, instead of standing
    frozen mid-stride

Fixed bugs
  - IDKFA no longer hands over weapons the loaded set could never select:
    the super shotgun in DOOM 1, and the plasma rifle and BFG in shareware
  - running into a wall no longer collects an item sealed behind it
  - a lift or door narrower than a monster no longer moves straight through
    one standing at its edge, pinning it in mid-air
  - a crate's top cropped its texture mid-face: it now starts at the 
    structure's own corner, on the face its walls show
  - the camera orbit no longer sticks between two 45° steps: taking a replay
    over mid-turn snaps it back, and a save stores where the turn was heading
  - shooting a wall under an open sky leaves its bullet puff again
  - a crusher's blood spray drew its randomness only where the set had the
    sprite for it, so a replay desynced against a set missing BLUD


===============================================================================

v0.18.1 (2026-09-07)

Features and improvements
  - replays now play back identically in every browser: 
    the simulation computes sin/cos/atan2/exp/log itself instead of asking 
    the engine, which rounds them differently from one version to the next
  - the replay bar no longer notes the engine a replay was recorded on
  - improved monster-AI performance, most noticable on monster-heavy maps
  - improved renderer performance:
    - sprites draw from a texture atlas: a few draw calls a frame instead of 
      one per lump, and the atlas frees the decoded art it packed (~18 MB)
    - dynamic lights are also more efficient now, so I also raised their limit

Fixed bugs
  - a dynamic light could skip a leaf in plain sight, flickering with 
    the light's radius
  - seeking a replay past a keyframe desynced the run: sleeping monsters
    woke up to 10 tics off, and a fire chain in flight was lost
  - a monster restored next to a teleporter could fire it on the first tic
    after the load, without having walked over it
  - seeking a replay forwards showed the messages the jump passed over 
    (a secret found, a locked door) as if they had just happened


===============================================================================

v0.18.0 (2026-09-06)

REPLAYS! A run can be recorded and played back, in this engine's own format.
Changes to the gameplay simulation break existing replays (desync), so the
next point releases will focus on getting that stable.

Savegames made in previous versions are silently broken, as I didn't 
raised SAVE_VERSION yet (this mechanism is for post-1.0).

Features and improvements
  - Replays:
    - new "Replays" tab to organize recordings
    - start recording with a new game (a checkbox on New Game) or mid-level
      from the replays tab
    - replays can be watched like videos, including seeking
    - the player name a replay is credited to is entered on the replay itself
      and inherited by later recordings
    - taking a replay over, flags that level as "cheated"
    - replays copied into public/game/replay/ are listed on the tab as
      "included": playable and downloadable, but not editable
  - Menu:
    - "Start new game" and a save's "Load" have to be held while a game is
      running, so a stray click can't throw the level away
    - the status line is cleared when you switch tabs
    - the save, load and replay lists have a filter field beside their heading
    - a welcome popup at boot
  - Rendering:
    - thin ceilings are trimmed to reduce visual clutter
    - distance lighting: surfaces and sprites darken with their
      depth from the camera, smoothly through the COLORMAP ramp
  - Save- and Replay files:
    - an unnamed save or replay is named after the WAD its map came from and
      the map: "DOOM2 MAP05", "NUTS MAP01"
    - a downloaded save is named after the save, as a replay is, and carries
      its own ".topdoomsave.json" suffix
    - savegames and replay snapshots store only the THINGs that are no longer
      as the map spawned them (this is why saves broke here)
    - a save or replay of a PWAD map plays on another IWAD, when the one it
      was made with is gone
    - a thing the WAD set has no sprite for is now said on screen, not only in
      the console

Fixed bugs
  - fixed some auto-aim problems
  - a rising lift or floor no longer pins a monster in geometry
  - a monster standing beside a ledge taller than a step no longer levitates
    onto it when it wakes and hovers there (the two shotgun guys on E1M1)
  - a long menu status line no longer squeezes the footer buttons until their
    labels wrap


===============================================================================

v0.17.1 (2026-09-03)

Some smaller improvements and fixes before I begin with REPLAYS!
Because I changed how the settings are saved, yours get resetted now, sry!

Features and improvements
  - Settings:
    - all settings live in one localStorage entry now; settings stored by an
      earlier build are NOT migrated and start out at their defaults again
    - the frame limit defaults to 60 fps
  - DEHACKED:
    - MBF's 109 extra states and 107 extra sprite names are there, and
      a patch addressing a frame past them grows the table
    - a weapon whose fire chain is repointed at another firing action
      fires that weapon's shot - patch-built weapons like nosp4.wad's 
      Super Rocket Launcher work
    - the weapon-matching player skin follows a patched weapon's shot, and 
      stands down entirely where no shipped skin depicts what a weapon fires

Fixed bugs
  - a map an PWAD replaced is no longer named after the IWAD's level of 
    that name
  - knockback no longer shoves a monster off a ledge its own walk step
    refuses, leaving it standing on air over the drop
  - a DEHACKED monster whose attack is repointed at a refire chain now hoses 
    without pause like the chain's owner, instead of firing one burst 
    and walking off
  - a BEX [SOUNDS] key that names no sfx is reported instead of counted
    as a redirect that landed


===============================================================================

v0.17.0 (2026-09-02)

Heading towards v1.0 in big steps.
But there will be an v0.18 before, then polishing and bug-fixing.

Features and improvements
  - UDMF maps load (needs ZNODES): the doom namespace plays in full, ZDoom
    namespaces are flagged red but stay pickable (geometry yes, specials no)
  - visual improvements / eye candy - most toggleable in Settings / Visuals:
    - the void around the level draws as slowly drifting fog instead of black
    - ambient occlusion: floors darken toward the walls standing on them
    - areas open to the sky are tinted toward the level's own sky texture
    - bloom: torches, lamps and plasma leave a soft glow on the frame
      (off by default — it is not cheap)
    - a subtle blob shadow under the player
  - weapon-matching player skins! Doomguy only, but can be forced for WADs
    which customize the player sprites, all tuneable in Settings / Visuals
  - mover interpolation: moveable areas draw interpolated between tics 
    instead of stepping at 35 Hz
  - maps are now divided into "islands": Only the current island is visible, 
    so areas seperated from the current one (fake "room-over-room" areas 
    accessed by silent teleports etc.) stay invisible
  - a corpse under a door, floor or crusher is squashed to a pool of blood
    - a crusher sprays blood out of whoever it is grinding
    - a DEH patch repointing S_GIBS moves the pool with it
  - a crowd of monsters waking at once no longer floods the sound channels
  - starting a game shows a loading screen with the WAD download's progress
  - menu / WAD Library: 
    - a WAD with a .txt beside it gets an info icon; clicking it reads the file
    - shortened 'DEHACKED' to 'DEH'
    - a support tooltip names at most 3 maps per reason, sorted

Fixed bugs
  - aiming and shooting:
    - a monster shooting through a window now aims through it, like the player
      does, instead of firing into its frame
    - a monster's shot sits at the original's own heights: a hitscan leaves at
      its species' fire height, a fireball 32 units up at both ends
    - weapon projectiles now leave the body instead of the player's head
    - shots no longer slip through a crusher that has come down
  - knockback is now capped: a BFG-hit corpse no longer rockets out of the map
  - a silent teleporter no longer strands a camera turn (Q/E) part-way through
  - the camera yaw wraps at ±180° instead of counting up
  - fixed some floors standing 4 units past a wall 
    (BSP related stuff - don't ask me)


