v0.16.1 (2026-08-27)

Features and improvements
  - add 3 of the classic cheat codes
    - a cheated run sets no best times, and its intermission screen says
      "You cheated" instead of showing the level's stats
  - further optimized wall fading performance
  - the crosshair keeps a solid black outline, so it stays readable over
    bright floors and fire
  - blue on health/armor and the crosshair is brighter
  - a focused text field or dropdown takes the menu's accent, not the 
    browser's focus ring
  - profiler overlay and fps count can be switched on/off in any environment: 
    Settings -> General -> Debug / Dev (off by default)
  - new app- and favicon
  - best times moved from localStorage into IndexedDB; existing times are
    migrated on the next visit

Fixed bugs
  - monsters with a melee attack no longer hurt you the instant you touch
    them: a claw lands a windup later
    - backing out of reach during that windup makes the swing miss; an imp,
      cacodemon or baron throws its fireball after you instead
  - a teleported monster stands on the floor it arrives at instead of falling
    to it from the height of the closet it left
  - a voodoo doll parked in damaging floor no longer bleeds the player
  - a spectre behind a fading wall no longer strobes in and out of view
  - a flying monster spawned against a block too low to sit on no longer
    pops up onto it and hangs there for the rest of the level


===============================================================================

v0.16.0 (2026-08-26)

Features and improvements
  - walls and floors fade as a soft ball around whatever they hide, instead
    of whole panels
    - a monster far from the player fades less than one right beside them
    - a raised floor only fades where the sightline actually lands on it
    - the fade aims at the whole sprite, not its middle
    - each monster is aimed at over its own height, so a tall one is no
      longer half-hidden by what a player-sized target would have cleared
  - dynamic lights: torches, lamps, pickups, projectiles in flight, 
    explosions and muzzle flashes now light the level around them
    - a WAD's own GLDEFS/DOOMDEFS lump layers over the stock definitions
    - Settings > Visuals > Lighting turns them off
  - massive auto-camera overhaul
  - main menu:
    - F2 / F3 / F4 open the menu on the Save / Load / Settings tab
    - switching game WAD keeps the add-ons it can't merge: 
      they stay in the list switched off, with the reason on the row
    - Settings is split four ways: Visuals, Audio, Controls, and General
    - implemented a master volume slider
  - the HUD's numbers now use DOOMs digit sprites
    - crosshair uses the same blue than the one used for health/armor > 100
  - map-mesh and rendering optimizations: big maps cost a lot less per frame
  - multisampling is off on high-DPI displays, where it cost a third of every
    frame to smooth edges already drawn at four pixels apiece
  - the profiler shows GPU time beside CPU time
  - basic SEO: the page carries its own metadata now

Fixed bugs
  - an item in an alcove raised too high to step into is collected now
  - a voodoo doll carried over an item now collects it for the player
  - a PWAD's eight sprite rotations now beat the IWAD's rotation-0 view for the
    same frame (NoSp3's Cybruiser attacked and flinched as a Wolfenstein SS)


