v0.15.1 (2026-08-22)

Features and improvements
  - HEXEN-format maps load: HEXEN itself is not planned, but some
    community maps use that format. 
    These maps will not play right, but at least they dont render 
    as garbage geometry now.
  - WAD Library:
    - add a support column says whether a file runs fully,
      only partly (HEXEN format, or a DEHACKED this engine won't fully
      apply) or not at all (UDMF, GL nodes, no nodes).
      A tooltip tells the reasons and the maps that raise them.
    - a file with no map this engine can load can't be picked any more
    - your own WAD folder is rescanned at startup, so files added
      since the last visit show up without opening the overlay
  - Menues: "Press-and-hold to confirm" buttons act a bit faster now


===============================================================================

v0.15.0 (2026-08-21)

Features and improvements
  - WAD Library: browse your own WAD folder from the menu, remembered between
    visits, replacing the two "from disk" buttons
  - DEHACKED/BEX patches are read and applied
    - supported:
      - level titles, par times, monster stats
      - ammo counts and caps, the starting kit, the health and armour limits,
        and the BFG's cells per shot
      - weapon records whole: ammo class, five frame pointers, fire rate
      - which lump a sound or a music track resolves to
      - the death overlay's killer line
      - the locked-door and locked-switch lines
      - frame records and a Thing's frame pointers, by re-deriving the sprite
        lists and attack/pain timings from the patched frame table
      - [SPRITES] and Text sprite renames
    - not yet supported:
      - action pointers (Pointer, [CODEPTR])
    - a save made with a patch loaded now requires that file back, since without
      it every patched stat would silently revert
  - fullbright frames: torches, keys, powerups, projectiles, explosions and
    firing frames now draw at full light, as vanilla's frame table says
  - some work on the intermission screen
    - now shows the level's par time, green if you beat it
    - now shows a face for how the level went, based on your stats
  - the death overlay is drawn in the WAD's own font, like the other cards

Fixed bugs
  - spider mastermind, cyberdemon and arachnotron now walk at vanilla's speed
  - monsters wind up before firing, as vanilla does: a shot lands partway into
    the attack instead of the instant the monster decides to
  - a resurrected monster now plays its whole raise sequence
  - the cyberdemon's three rockets come 24 tics apart, not 12
  - a barrel's blast comes 15 tics after death, not 10


===============================================================================

v0.14.3 (2026-08-20)

Some fixes and minor improvements before starting DEH/BEX support.

Features and improvements
  - various "underwater" improvements:
    - the view no longer turns blue when the player wades under a 242 water
      surface; the camera stays above it, so the tint only read as a bug
    - a water surface no longer breaks up over a submerged player: it is already
      translucent, so occlusion fading has nothing to reveal there

Fixed bugs
  - resolved some problems with doors and switches:
    - a door reopened after a close line no longer shuts itself again a few
      seconds later
    - close-door lines close straight away instead of pausing at the top first
    - pressing use on an open door now shuts it, as in vanilla, instead of
      restarting its wait
    - a lift triggered a second time now uses that line's speed and re-reads how
      far down it goes, instead of repeating its first trigger
  - solid sectors (pillars, mapper-made blocks) are no longer left dark forever
    by the fog of war, which drew them as holes in the level
  - a stair step built up out of deep water keeps the pool bottom's flat and
    light instead of turning into a patch of water
  - a sector walled in by a pool no longer leaves a hole in the water surface
    over it (BOOMEDIT MAP01 sector 121)



