===============================================================================

v0.14.0 (2026-08-18)

Features and improvements
  - initial BOOM compatibility
    - generalized linedefs and sector types, extended linedef numbers,
      six-slot keys and generalized locks, elevators, extended BSP nodes
    - silent and line-to-line teleporters, instant toggle floors
    - a WAD's own ANIMATED and SWITCHES tables are used when it ships them
    - a sector can now run a floor and a ceiling special at the same time,
      as BOOM does
    - scrolling walls, floors and ceilings, including the ones a moving
      sector drives or accelerates
    - conveyor belts, which carry all types of objects
    - icy and muddy floors: friction changes how you accelerate and how
      fast you end up going, and how far a hit slides you
    - wind, currents and point pushers that shove or pull you across a room
    - voodoo dolls: a map's extra player starts now walk lines and take
      damage on your behalf, so conveyor-driven scripts run
    - deep water: a pool drawn at another sector's height, with a
      see-through surface you stay visible under while wading
      - and water that rises and falls when the sector driving it moves
    - a sector can borrow another's lighting for its floor or its ceiling,
      so a lava pit lights itself and whatever stands in it
    - see-through midtextures
    - a BOOM map's own colormaps tint the whole view while you stand in the
      sector that names them
  - a monster killed mid-knockback now slides to a stop instead of freezing
    where it died
  - solid structures are no longer see-through holes in the level. 
    This change came in by accident, but may be nice
  - increased view distance
  - sexy scrollbars for the menues
  - finding a secret plays its own chime instead of a borrowed WAD sound

Fixed bugs
  - fixed various rendering problems


===============================================================================

v0.13.0 (2026-08-16)

Features and improvements
  - MUSIC! 
    - MUS and MIDI lumps both play, using OPL2/OPL3 emulation driven by 
      the WAD's own GENMIDI instrument bank
    - Ogg/FLAC/MP3/WAV lump from a music-replacement PWAD plays natively
    - a WAD's MAPINFO can name a level's music, and the intermission gets its
      own track like it does in vanilla
    - Music volume slider in the settings menu, beside the sound effects one.
    - default volumes: 80% for sound and 60% for music
  - telefragging: teleporting onto something kills it instantly
  - improved projectile tracer animation
  - darker areas are slightly darker now
  - minor menu layout improvements
  - booting the game shows a "Loading..." message, instead of the 
    empty HUD overlay

Fixed bugs
  - monster closets no longer give themselves away: the teleport fog (and any
    other effect) in a room you have never seen is hidden by the fog of war,
    like the monsters standing in it.
  - the monster counter no longer reads over 100% after an arch-vile
    resurrection: a raised monster now adds one to the level's monster total
    (ZDoom's rule), so clearing the level ends at exactly 100% again


