v0.12.3 (2026-08-15)

Mostly internal refactoring and cleanup.

Features and improvements
  - dying on a level you loaded or saved on: R now takes you back to that
    savegame, instead to the start of the level

Fixed bugs
  - levels that end with an monster/icon-of-sin death trigger now work
    as intended... I think
  - fixed "You died!" screen appears, even if death is level-exit condition

Next Stop: Music, and BOOM compat! Also some visual stuff.


===============================================================================

v0.12.2 (2026-08-14)

Features and improvements
  - collision now clips the original's axis-aligned box instead of a
    circle, so you fit exactly where a DOOM marine fits
  - sight checks now honour the level's own REJECT table, the way the
    original does - cheaper on crowded maps, and a map that uses the
    table to blind its monsters on purpose now gets what it asked for
  - the settings menu is split into "General" and "Controls"
    - in "General" you can now toggle the profiler overlay (if DEVMODE)
  - monsters no longer block you from a height you'd never touch them at
    - the original blocks over the full height regardless ("infinitely
      tall actors"); "General" has a setting to put that back

Fixed bugs
  - coming back to a weapon slot selects the weapon you last used out
    of it, instead of always the stronger one of the two
  - an attacking monster now holds its attack pose for as long as the
    attack takes, instead of dropping back to standing partway through


===============================================================================

v0.12.1 (2026-08-13)

Features and improvements
  - secret exits work
    - a PWAD can define its own with MAPINFO's "next" / "secretnext"
  - the difficulty you pick now changes more than which monsters are
    placed, all of it as in the original
    - "I'm Too Young to Die" halves the damage you take
    - "I'm Too Young to Die" and "Nightmare!" double every ammo pickup
    - "Nightmare!" speeds up some monsters and their projectiles
    - "Nightmare!" respawns killed monsters back
  - if a game can't be saved (dead, intermission), the "Save"
    and "Overwrite" buttons are disabled now
  - loading a savegame no longer demands every add-on that happened to
    be loaded when it was made - only the game WAD and whichever file
    provided the level itself
    - a save whose game WAD or level file is gone now greys its "Load"
      button out instead of failing on the click
  - the savegame list is no longer capped at 24 entries
  - tuned (auto-)aiming

Fixed bugs
  - the camera drifted whenever the mouse passed over a monster
  - fixed getting stuck at the outside corner of a wall
  - spectres were drawn as ordinary demons; they now shimmer as the
    original's fuzz effect, corpses included
  - a monster whose step was clear but whose first fraction of it
    grazed a corner stood there forever
  - the super shotgun reloaded silently
  - manually named savegames can contain spaces now
  - fixed hairline cracks in the floor where two subsectors of the same
    sector meet (rare, but noteicable)


===============================================================================

v0.12.0 (2026-08-12)

Features and improvements
  - the game now simulates at a fixed 35 ticks per second, like the original
  - randomness now comes from DOOM's own random table instead of the
    browser's generator
  - SAVEGAMES! new Save and Load tabs in the menu
    - entering a level also writes an auto-save, and dying and pressing R
      restarts the level from it
  - the death screen now says what killed you
  - camera instantly snaps above the player when entering a level, 
    loading a save, or after an teleport
  - increased sound channels from 16 to 32

Fixed bugs
  - broken and flickering lights now behave like vanilla's
  - fixed problems with switches
    - a switch that did nothing, because every sector it targets was already
      busy, is no longer used up by the press
    - a one-shot switch now stays lit up after you press it
  - fixed some problems with crushers
  - monsters now use their real per-type body height (56 to 110) instead of one
    shared 64 everywhere
  - you can no longer step off a raised lift into a space whose ceiling sits
    below the lift's floor (DOOM2 MAP06)


===============================================================================

v0.11.0 (2026-08-10)

Features and improvements
  - add setting to cap the frame rate at 30, 60 or 120 fps
    (default: uncapped); it applies to the running level right away
  - increased view distance
  - bundled DOOM1 shareware is now the v1.9 one (I assume)
  - some HUD / UI work
    - entering a level now shows "Entering <level name>" on screen.
      - the name is the WAD's own CWILV/WILV graphic where it has one for that
        level, as drawn on the original's intermission screen
      - otherwise it comes from the WAD's own MAPINFO if it has one,
        otherwise from the hard-coded level titles from vanilla
      - a PWAD map with neither is named after the file it came from
      - the menu's level list shows those names too
    - leaving a level now shows an intermission popup
      - it now also tracks your best time per level, and announces a new one
        - records are kept per WAD, level and difficulty, and survive a reload
      - the WAD is identified by a hash of its contents, so renaming a file
        keeps its records and two different WADs sharing a name don't collide
      - a run started with ?pos= can't set a record
    - a locked door or switch now tells which key it requires
    - the HUD's weapon column has now a fixed width
    - the menu's CHANGELOG link, under the version number, opens this file
  - tuned scaling of pickup-items

Fixed bugs
  - projectiles now collide the way vanilla's do
    - rockets, plasma and BFG balls hit whatever they actually fly into,
      re-checked every frame
    - every shot is now tested against each monster's real size instead of
      one shared 24-unit hitbox
    - monster fireballs no longer hit from a body-width away or from far
      over your head
    - a shot passing you at speed can no longer slip between two frames
  - cacodemons, lost souls and pain elementals now really fly
  - monster walk animations now use each type's own frames
  - a THING the WAD set has no sprite for is still skipped, but the level
    load now logs which ones (it used to vanish without a word)
  - fixed periods, commas, hyphens and underscores in on-screen WAD-font text
  - fixed stuck monsters
  - fixed the game freezing when a second WAD is started from the menu after
    already having played a level


